 River below Granite Reef Dam is\nimminent or occurring. Flooding of low water crossings across the\nSalt River upstream of Tempe Town Lake, including McKellips Road,\nis imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 517 AM MST, SRP was releasing 1650 cfs from Granite Reef Dam.\nFlooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSalt River between Granite Reef Dam and Tempe Town Lake.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLWPSR"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS45 KPSR 311217"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING IN EFFECT UNTIL 2 PM MST THIS AFTERNOON"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KPSR.FA.W.0012.261031T1217Z-261031T2100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-10-31T14:00:00-07:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b573f3b6024e8eedf76c067f272e3b93357ea3a2.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-81.5,29.08],[-81.69,29.32],[-81.57,29.35],[-81.42,29.1],[-81.5,29.08]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b573f3b6024e8eedf76c067f272e3b93357ea3a2.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b573f3b6024e8eedf76c067f272e3b93357ea3a2.001.1","areaDesc":"Lake, FL; Volusia, FL","geocode":{"SAME":["012069","012127"],"UGC":["FLC069","FLC127"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC069","https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/FLC127"],"references":[{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.847a1488c7b13091f639b46dbc0d2074ce9c067f.001.1","identifier":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.847a1488c7b13091f639b46dbc0d2074ce9c067f.001.1","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-10-30T21:02:00-04:00"}],"sent":"2026-10-31T10:46:00-04:00","effective":"2026-10-31T10:46:00-04:00","onset":"2026-10-31T10:46:00-04:00","expires":"2026-10-31T23:45:00-04:00","ends":null,"status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Observed","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Melbourne FL","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 31 at 10:46AM EDT by NWS Melbourne FL","description":"...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in Florida...\n\nSt Johns River Near Astor affecting Volusia and Lake Counties.\n\n.Persistent northeast winds and downstream tidal effects on the St\nJohn River have slowed flow at Astor. Forecast rainfall may lead to\nadditional rises within Moderate flood stage.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Astor...Moderate flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Moderate flooding is occurring and is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Astor.\n\n* WHEN...Until further notice.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 3.5 feet, Canals have overflowed into yards. Homes on\nor near Wildhog and Bonnet roads become inaccessible with several\ninches of water inside homes along the river and canals. Docks at\nAstor Bridge marina and throughout Astor are completely submerged.\nBartram Rd and Holiday Circle are inaccessible with yards\ncompletely submerged. Clair Street is inaccessible. Roads flooded\nin South Moon Fish Camp, docks and yards at condominiums on Juno\nTrail and water breaches the sea wall at Blair's Jungle Den.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 9:30 AM EDT Saturday the stage was 3.5 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 9:30 AM EDT Saturday was 3.7 feet.\n- Forecast...Forecast rainfall may lead to additional rises within\nModerate Flood Stage.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued this evening at 1145 PM EDT.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 311446"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0003.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b17471914b8565dfa339052a1a87ce08a6538769.001.1,2026-10-30T11:15:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2a9e7fac7b5c5ad78bd2e1cf1fc774708f767f2.002.1,2026-10-29T21:03:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1840da910b02e49f40570094c2ce4d840da0f7e7.002.1,2026-10-29T09:16:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c7fdda2979f0f8f25569f6cde0da27cc8358a302.001.1,2026-10-28T21:31:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9aeb600074fc600db94b853bee79670c058b0e1e.001.1,2026-10-28T08:58:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6ac5f73e45906a0316f1b511e8afe3a3e5231ec2.001.1,2026-10-27T21:00:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.32a6624b03ca4bdc3923c468120fbeec7a6da027.002.1,2026-10-27T10:04:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.773baaf5fa5d14abca39f5240afdf228afff977d.001.1,2026-10-26T21:20:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6395ac22474085b0afc80efae484acd913f69a78.001.1,2026-10-26T09:55:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.216e8d1b705d46993d7c471c0b3a234344c7fb99.001.1,2026-10-25T21:25:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.15287a9048d637138112ab20fdb0596b03366bc8.001.1,2026-10-25T14:15:00-04:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.